  "inscriptions": [
    {
      "inscription": "1. ṹ deyadharmmoyaṃ laḍitagrāme yaṃgvalvihāre śā[kya] bhikṣuṇyā  \n2. pariśuddhamatyā yadattra puṇyaṃ tadbhavatu sarvvasatvānā-  \n3. manuttarasarvva jñānāvāptaye/ / saṃvat  \n4a. 500 10 3/ / caityakūta jinabandhuvihārapūrvva-bhuddeśe  \n4b. piṇḍakena bhojanaṃ karttavya*/ /  \n*Mistake for karttavyam",
      "inscription_translation": "This [image] is the pious gift of the Shakya nun Parishuddamati who lives in the Yamgval convent in Laditagrama. Whatever merit there may be in this [deed], may it lead to the attainment of supreme enlightenment of all sentient beings. Samvat 513 (AD 591). A feast should be provided [from the proceeds of] pindaka at the locale east of the Chaityakuta Jinabandhu monastery.",
      "inscription_remark": "Gautama Vajracharya (at LACMA 1975) once offered an alternate interpretation of the last line:  \"(It is the wish) that (a certain ascetic) Purnnaka, belonging to the monastery in the locality of Chaityakuta, should be fed.\"",
      "sortorder": null
    }
  ],
